{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1780956483,"nonce":"MWueYf9jg6o/Ah298/tFHcdPZbE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABEzGbHA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/239","origin":"github"},"title":"Post-deployment analysis: 2026-06-08 — first student operations day","message":"## Context\n\n**2026-06-08 was the first day students operated BizzyBoat** (Summer Hydro). The\nteam **ran over the VPN (BenCloud) all day** to work around flakiness on the\nWiFi bridge / operator network. Several networking issues caused **minor\noperational problems** during student ops. This issue tracks the post-deployment\nanalysis; the detailed record lives in\n`docs/logs/2026/2026-06-08_dev_logs.md`.\n\nThis is the first student-operations day following the 2026-06-05 pre-class\nshakedown (#228).\n\n## Issues observed (summary — detail + evidence in the log)\n\n- **Flaky `p11.lan` DNS / intermittent \"can't reach by name.\"** Root cause: the\n  operator Teltonika RUTX11 (`192.168.13.1`) WAN was configured as a **50/50\n  load-balance** between the stable wired `wan` and a **flapping WiFi WAN\n  (`ifWan1` / `wlan1-2`)**. Each WAN flap forced a dnsmasq reload → transient\n  resolution failures; half of upstream queries also rode the dying link.\n  **Mitigation applied:** WiFi WAN disabled (now single-WAN — see follow-ups).\n- **`eth0.4` DHCP log spam** on the operator router — the **boat-side OmniTIK is\n  set to DHCP-client** on the all-static `172.16.20.0/24` bridge (no DHCP server\n  there by design), so it broadcasts DISCOVERs every 1–3 s forever. Cosmetic +\n  minor load. Fix is boat-side (static IP on the OmniTIK).\n- **mercat \"unreachable\" was a false alarm** — Windows Firewall blocks inbound\n  ICMP; the host is reachable via SSH/services. Pinging it is a misleading health\n  check.\n- **Shore SXTsq Lite5 radio had a stale RouterBOOT** (6.45.9 under RouterOS\n  7.22); upgraded + rebooted. RF link itself is healthy (−43 dBm, CCQ 95/100%).\n- **salmon → shore radio (`172.16.20.4`) reachability gap — UNRESOLVED.** salmon\n  can't reach the radio despite routing identical to deadpool (which can).\n\n## Follow-ups / action items\n\n- [ ] Re-add WAN failover the correct way: WiFi WAN as a **lower-metric backup**\n      behind wired `wan` (not 50/50 balance) — and diagnose why `wlan1-2` flaps\n      before re-enabling.\n- [ ] Boat-side: set the OmniTIK to a **static IP** on `172.16.20.0/24` to stop\n      the `eth0.4` DHCP spam.\n- [ ] Close out the **salmon → `172.16.20.4`** reachability gap.\n- [ ] Decide whether to capture VPN-vs-WiFi operating posture for future student days.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}